// Issue #319: the call-stack-overflow fatal fast path
// (spec/04-semantics.md, "Call stack overflow's fatal fast path") must
// skip every pending deferred call too, the same way any other fatal
// fault does — no `try` statement is active anywhere in this program, so
// native never reaches the catchable StackOverflowError construction at
// all (src/vm.cpp VM::call()). This is not issue #326: that issue is
// about a stack overflow a live `try` statement catches; this program has
// no `try` statement at all. Both managed backends must agree: empty
// stdout, no "d" lines. An error_probes entry in
// tools/check_jvm_probes.sh and tools/check_clr_probes.sh.
fun note(s) { print s; }
fun rec(n) { defer note("d"); return rec(n + 1); }
rec(0);
